[{:db/id "q-332642/selection/7e0716ee44c4440b56499b93cfa0fd82154bb47dec80337819c9a11e6734f41b" :answer/id #uuid "31e3904a-5f7e-5ee1-a988-b95ef10c18d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332642/selection/f190e41a5b4298afc409d4fc5ab1eaba4deca07f5ec856300aa60fcb1b4621f4" :answer/id #uuid "88fdfd9a-0542-54cd-8bd0-97f7295dd38b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332642/selection/0bf48b8ef873df18a23a93510256f82fc38db7145b11309a9899dafdd7ff95ae" :answer/id #uuid "bde16033-6d8e-56b7-9177-9544dce2a482" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{-6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332642/selection/273cf6c29e8963346e69ff835b6c3454527d0b9ce8ff0c226c8f8b1be0f49008" :answer/id #uuid "494a2cad-3f27-5942-81b8-1a52d437480c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332642/selection/81b0abd37faec18752dd0680dc5d8749459665100cfde64af75643f93934485e" :answer/id #uuid "20210690-7c1f-5517-88ec-e7a794d092fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332642/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e79819bf-0bc6-5d97-8d52-938c841cfb1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332642/selection/0bf48b8ef873df18a23a93510256f82fc38db7145b11309a9899dafdd7ff95ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-332642/selection/7e0716ee44c4440b56499b93cfa0fd82154bb47dec80337819c9a11e6734f41b" "q-332642/selection/f190e41a5b4298afc409d4fc5ab1eaba4deca07f5ec856300aa60fcb1b4621f4" "q-332642/selection/0bf48b8ef873df18a23a93510256f82fc38db7145b11309a9899dafdd7ff95ae" "q-332642/selection/273cf6c29e8963346e69ff835b6c3454527d0b9ce8ff0c226c8f8b1be0f49008" "q-332642/selection/81b0abd37faec18752dd0680dc5d8749459665100cfde64af75643f93934485e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332642" :question/id #uuid "28806fbf-9dcd-5e9c-ad17-59ce05f99707" :question/math-academy-id "q-332642" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+6y=-5{x}^{2}+4x-7.\n$$\n\nFind the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)$ to this equation, where $A$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "To find the complementary solution, we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+6{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that this differential equation is separable since we can write it as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}=-6{y}_{c}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}_{c}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}=-6\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}_{c}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}_{c}}\\,\\text{d}{y}_{c} & =\\int -6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|{y}_{c}| & =-6x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we make ${y}_{c}$ the subject by exponentiating both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{y}_{c}| & ={e}^{-6x+C} \\\\  & ={e}^{-6x}{e}^{C} \\\\  & =K{e}^{-6x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}.$ \n\nFinally, we can drop the absolute value by allowing the arbitrary constant to be either positive or negative, i.e., setting $A=\\pm K.$  Therefore, the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-6x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332642/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77ba8502-9ddb-52d0-a885-33190dc04d4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332642"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332695/selection/7e0716ee44c4440b56499b93cfa0fd82154bb47dec80337819c9a11e6734f41b" :answer/id #uuid "b85afa91-a789-5a8a-883c-1b338b975502" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/